      },
      "summary": "The change covers the main logging and trace redaction paths, but formatted values for sensitive properties can remain in emitted log messages when formatting changes their text representation.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/RedactionFilter.cs",
          "line": 43,
          "message": "Formatted sensitive values can bypass message redaction when the template applies a format specifier.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RedactingLogger.Log formats the original state, then RenderMessage tries to remove sensitive values by replacing each value's unformatted ToString() in the formatted message. The structured property is redacted separately, but the formatted message is sent to the provider too.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs a numeric passcode with a format specifier, such as `logger.LogInformation(\"Passcode {passcode:X}\", 4815)`. The formatter emits `12CF`, while the replacement searches for `4815`, so the passcode remains in the log message. This violates the requirement to redact sensitive properties before they leave the process (OWASP A09:2025)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
      "reviewType": "testing",
